<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Russian State</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1920 CE · capital Omsk</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The White government of Admiral Kolchak, based in Omsk, which claimed to rule all of Russia against the Bolsheviks in 1918 to 1920.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In September 1918 anti-Bolshevik groups meeting at Ufa created an All-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-provisional-government">Russian Provisional Government</a>, a five-member Directory led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikolai-avksentiev">Nikolai Avksentiev</a>. Based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omsk">Omsk</a>, it called its territory the Russian State. On 18 November 1918 officers overthrew the Directory and made Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-kolchak">Alexander Kolchak</a> Supreme Ruler.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-kolchak">Kolchak</a> ruled as a military dictator, and other White leaders, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin">Denikin</a>, formally recognised his authority. His government controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ural-mountains">Urals</a> and held most of the Russian gold reserve. Its armies advanced towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> in spring 1919, but reprisals, corruption and failure to win over peasants undermined it.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> counter-attacked, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omsk">Omsk</a> fell in November 1919. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-kolchak">Kolchak</a> was handed over by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovak-legion">Czechoslovak Legion</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irkutsk">Irkutsk</a> and shot in February 1920. Remnants of his forces retreated to the Far East.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/russian-state.jpg" alt="Russian State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Peter the Great · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Russia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Omsk</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nikolai Avksentiev, Alexander Kolchak, Viktor Pepelyayev</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Russia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kolchak government, White Russia (1918-1920)</dd></dl></aside></div>

